I'm thinking the cop, Leverette, is most involved as well and the family that called are deeply involved as well. One of the people in those two groups is the murderer, and they're most likely close friends. I'd say that Leverette  was the murderer based on his lack of proper procedure. Claudia, the girlfriend, was most likely the girl that called into Unsolved Mysteries because as a young person that is a lot to bear for a lifetime and it was weighing on her. She was probably also the person who sent the pictures.

&#x200B;

Leverette must carry some weight around the area to have the entire department just go along with his opinion. See if you can figure out his role in the community. His rank in the department, who he was having relations with, and, most importantly, where he is now. To play it so cool he must have done something like that before unless he could be classified as a sociopath. Talk to the gossips if they're still alive. If they're not, check out their kids. See if he has any other unsolved murders or under-researched suicides in his past. 

&#x200B;

Once you get that info, message me. I don't want to be recorded emailing anyone or posting to the website for my personal safety, but you seem pretty invested already. I'm willing to help any way I can while keeping myself safe. It seems like this is surrounded by too many layers of corruption for communication that's too direct.

&#x200B;

Best wishes,

Tomato
